{"name":"Intoxication","hex":"#a1ac4d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"intoxication","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A poisoning, as by a spirituous or a narcotic substance.","The state of being intoxicated or drunk."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intoxication"}],"entries":[{"title":"Substance intoxication","blocks":[{"text":"Substance intoxication is a transient condition of altered consciousness and behavior associated with recent use of a substance. It is often maladaptive and impairing, but reversible. If the symptoms are severe, the term \"substance intoxication delirium\" may be used. Slang terms for the state include: getting high (generic), and being stoned, cooked, or fried."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Substance_intoxication","wikidata":"Q865968"},{"title":"Alcohol intoxication","blocks":[{"text":"Alcohol intoxication, commonly described in higher doses as drunkenness or inebriation, and known in overdose as alcohol poisoning, is the behavior and physical effects caused by recent consumption of alcohol. The technical term intoxication in common speech may suggest that a large amount of alcohol has been consumed, leading to accompanying physical symptoms and deleterious health effects. Mild intoxication is mostly referred to by slang terms such as tipsy or buzzed. In addition to the toxicity of ethanol, the main psychoactive component of alcoholic beverages, other physiological symptoms may arise from the activity of acetaldehyde, a metabolite of alcohol. These effects may not arise until hours after ingestion and may contribute to a condition colloquially known as a hangover."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Michelangelo_drunken_Noah.jpg/330px-Michelangelo_drunken_Noah.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alcohol_intoxication","wikidata":"Q205972"},{"title":"Intoxication (Shaggy album)","blocks":[{"text":"Intoxication is the eighth studio album by Jamaican rapper Shaggy. It was released on 22 October 2007 through VP Records. Recording sessions took place at Big Yard Studios and Ranch Studio in New York, Jungle Studio and Judgement Yard Studio in Jamaica, The House and Circle House Studios in Florida. Production was handled by Sting Int'l, Tony \"CD\" Kelly, Christopher \"Longman\" Birch, Robert Livingston, Dwayne Shippy and Goldenchyl. It features guest appearances from Na'sha, Akon, Collie Buddz, Mischieve, Rayvon, Rik Rok, Sizzla and Tony Gold."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c9/Shaggy_-_Intoxicaton_-_Cover%28front%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Intoxication_(Shaggy_album)","wikidata":"Q1119637"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/The_wine_is_a_mocker_1663-1664_Jan_Steen.jpg/500px-The_wine_is_a_mocker_1663-1664_Jan_Steen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/The_wine_is_a_mocker_1663-1664_Jan_Steen.jpg/1280px-The_wine_is_a_mocker_1663-1664_Jan_Steen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/The_wine_is_a_mocker_1663-1664_Jan_Steen.jpg/500px-The_wine_is_a_mocker_1663-1664_Jan_Steen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Wine is a Mocker by Jan Steen c. 1663","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_wine_is_a_mocker_1663-1664_Jan_Steen.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/%28Five_stages_of_inebriation%2C_ca.1863-1868%29_-_photographer_Charles_Percy_Pickering_%289610229733%29_%282%29.jpg/500px-%28Five_stages_of_inebriation%2C_ca.1863-1868%29_-_photographer_Charles_Percy_Pickering_%289610229733%29_%282%29.jp